  <section|External tasks and active ownership><label|external-tasks-and-active-ownership>

  Trace sensor/weighted Ward limit <hlink|#33|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/33>
  owns <verbatim|trace-prosper-sensor.tex> and YM-000033. Branch limits/trace
  washout <hlink|#34|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/34>
  owns <verbatim|trace-branch-moments.tex> and YM-000034. Both external
  claims currently expire 13 November10:00UTC; recheck live discussions. Do
  not duplicate them or release those claims. Their author's submission
  restrictions remain in force.

  The independent clean-build audit <hlink|#37|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/37>
  has its own external claim through13 November11:00UTC and is not duplicated
  here. Earlier accepted source evidence used a verified prebuilt artifact
  and kernel replay; this checkpoint does not claim a new clean source build.

  The parent stopped at the 30% weekly-remaining threshold. Its claim release
  and final handoff commit are linked in issue26; this does not release
  external claims. Luna drafting agents and the independent Astra reviewer
  have stopped too. The final pass is reserved until the user explicitly
  requests it.

  <section|New checked local arguments><label|new-checked-local-arguments>

  Since the838-page checkpoint, the integrated draft adds physical Ward
  propagation, free internal Ward erasure, every-character compact Ward
  inheritance, harmonic collision-pole separation, exact radial/Euler Ward
  flux, original-null inclusion in each phase, the free external
  detector/quiet-vector classifier/finite collinear tests, the finite-volume
  shell-node producer, and literal-family Binding with paid-wait weakening.
  The classifier and shell candidates have been repaired and independently
  checked at recorded hashes.

  Each addition has a bounded independent review in <verbatim|reviews/> and
  source evidence. Cross-order kernel separation received an additional
  independent parent review; the Astra reviewer checked the complementary
  classifier arguments. These are local checks at stated inputs, not a
  certificate of global closure.

  <section|Remaining mathematical work><label|remaining-mathematical-work>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Literal-family Binding is now proved. The next C12/C13 audit must
    compare the actual exported Chateau rated/warrant/market outputs with the
    local compiler's inputs. An internal franchise receipt cannot be
    recovered for an already fixed run merely by reopening its existential
    construction, and may not be needed. Do not invent a separate Launch
    estimate or silently choose another family.

    <item>The physical Ward binding audit verifies per-grade finite-test
    scales, the common scalar by inclusion and the selected reference stress.
    Its analytic supplier closure remains part of the full audit, not a
    consequence of typing.

    <item>External trace33/34 remain necessary. Canonical YM-000022 running
    extraction needs its review response and explicit inclusion/application;
    do not duplicate its proof.

    <item>Whole dependency closure, exact public meaning/source audit,
    independent final reviews, literature/application audit and editorial
    work remain required.
  </itemize-minus>

  See <verbatim|endpoint-closure-ledger.md> for inspected public same-witness
  calls. The actual native R,T,W/history and fixed100 profile must be
  preserved. Alternate Roll/Novena/Ebb/Ariva/Meridian witnesses and
  historical centered-budget/production drafts are not missing public
  obligations. The final assembly is still conditional. Do not infer a
  mass-gap result or a broader generalized-free-field exclusion.

